{
  "_comment": "Target registry. Copy to config/targets.json (gitignored) and add YOUR repos. Each target has agents (review | docs-sync | qa | brain-sync); cadence is 'on-commit' or 'every:<dur>' (e.g. every:12h). brain-sync distills important changes into the shared Simbastack-hq/simbastack-brain repo as a PR — set BRAIN_PATH in config/sentinel.env, and use 'every:24h' (never 'on-commit'). ai_allowed gates sending a repo's code/DOM/diff to external models — set it deliberately for proprietary code.",
  "targets": {

    "_example_simple_webapp": {
      "path": "/Users/you/projects/my-simple-app",
      "github": "",
      "base": "main",
      "ai_allowed": true,
      "agents": {
        "qa": {
          "enabled": true,
          "cadence": "every:12h",
          "app": {
            "engine": "pi-native",
            "start_cmd": "node server.js",
            "port": 3000,
            "health_path": "/",
            "boot_timeout": 60,
            "max_steps": 10,
            "goal": "Describe what to exercise: upload a photo, submit a search, verify results render without JS errors, check empty/error states."
          }
        },
        "review": { "enabled": true, "cadence": "on-commit" },
        "docs-sync": { "enabled": false, "cadence": "on-commit" }
      }
    },

    "_example_fullstack_flow_engine": {
      "path": "/Users/you/projects/my-pms",
      "github": "your-org/my-pms",
      "base": "dev",
      "ai_allowed": true,
      "agents": {
        "qa": {
          "enabled": true,
          "cadence": "every:12h",
          "app": {
            "engine": "flow",
            "start_cmd": "pnpm dev",
            "set_port": false,
            "port": 3000,
            "aux_ports": [4000],
            "host": "localhost",
            "api_base": "http://localhost:4000",
            "boot_timeout": 120,
            "uiux_review": true,
            "plan_file": "",
            "pre_cmd": "",
            "post_cmd": "",
            "model": "",
            "provider": "",
            "thinking": "",
            "flow_max": "",
            "flow_attempts": "",
            "flow_steps": "",
            "seed_local_storage": {},
            "login": {
              "path": "/login",
              "email_env": "MYAPP_QA_EMAIL",
              "password_env": "MYAPP_QA_PASSWORD"
            }
          },
          "issues": {
            "_comment": "Optional: file each NEW functional bug as a GitHub issue (gh auth required). Dedup is persisted per target, so re-found bugs are never re-filed. plan_file (app, above) = hand-authored critical_flows JSON used verbatim (skips recon — for routers recon can't read, or curated flows). pre_cmd gates the run (nonzero exit aborts — e.g. a canary balance check); post_cmd always runs after the engine (e.g. a janitor).",
            "repo": "your-org/my-pms",
            "min_severity": "medium",
            "max_per_run": 5
          }
        },
        "pr-qa": {
          "_comment": "On-demand QA from a PR comment: a team member comments '/qa <what to test>' on an open PR → Sentinel resolves the PR's preview deployment (deployment status environment_url, else preview_url_template with {branch}), drives it with the comment as the goal (reusing this target's qa.app config), and posts one result comment on the PR. ALWAYS an unfunded burner + no issue filing, regardless of qa.app settings — PR branches are arbitrary code. preview_url_allow (host suffixes) is REQUIRED — pr-qa refuses to run without it, and only drives hosts matching a suffix. Run the QA host WITHOUT privileged reach into internal networks (see DESIGN §5d residual-risk note): URL string checks can't stop DNS rebinding or a browser following a redirect to an internal IP.",
          "enabled": false,
          "cadence": "every:5m",
          "repo": "your-org/my-pms",
          "command": "/qa",
          "allowed_associations": ["OWNER", "MEMBER", "COLLABORATOR"],
          "max_prs_per_tick": 1,
          "max_runs_per_pr_per_day": 4,
          "preview_url_template": "",
          "preview_url_allow": [".vercel.app"]
        },
        "review": { "enabled": false, "cadence": "on-commit" },
        "brain-sync": { "enabled": true, "cadence": "every:24h" }
      }
    },

    "_example_web3_wallet_dapp": {
      "_comment": "QA a wallet-gated dApp (MetaMask/Rabby). Sentinel injects an UNFUNDED burner wallet so the agent can connect + drive the UI WITHOUT touching app code; no transaction is ever broadcast (read-only RPC allow-list + deny-by-prefix + fail-closed preflight). The whitelist stub AES-encrypts the burner into the app's own NEXT_PUBLIC_CRYPTO_KEY (read from the QA .env) at the __WL_ADDR__ token. Optionally boot a branch where the gated UI is live, in a throwaway worktree. Use a local `anvil --fork-url` RPC if you want real on-chain execution with fake money.",
      "path": "/Users/you/projects/my-dapp",
      "github": "",
      "base": "main",
      "ai_allowed": true,
      "agents": {
        "qa": {
          "enabled": true,
          "cadence": "every:24h",
          "app": {
            "engine": "pi-native",
            "branch": "feature/live-ui",
            "worktree": true,
            "install_cmd": "yarn install --frozen-lockfile",
            "qa_env": "config/my-dapp.qa.env",
            "start_cmd": "yarn dev",
            "port": 3000,
            "host": "localhost",
            "health_path": "/app",
            "start_path": "/app",
            "boot_timeout": 180,
            "max_steps": 30,
            "uiux_review": true,
            "web3": {
              "enabled": true,
              "rpc": "https://arb1.arbitrum.io/rpc",
              "chain_id": 42161,
              "stubs": [
                { "url": "**/api/records*", "whitelist": true, "json": { "data": [{ "fields": { "Address": "__WL_ADDR__" } }] } },
                { "url": "**/api/country*", "json": { "message": "YES" } },
                { "url": "**/*.walletconnect.com/**", "abort": true }
              ]
            },
            "goal": "Connect the injected MetaMask wallet, then exercise the core flow. The burner is UNFUNDED, so on-chain submission failing with 'insufficient funds' is EXPECTED, not a bug — focus on rendering, quotes/validation, and how the UI handles the unfunded state. Ignore WalletConnect relay/socket console errors (QA-env artifact)."
          }
        },
        "review": { "enabled": false, "cadence": "on-commit" }
      }
    }

  }
}
